{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"760f640b2604d7651243e0270bb9761338e538b8fc726cc9dc572e8f5294427d","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler inbound fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","apply_inbound_records.py","projects_store.py","_build_snapshot","jqls_for","get_parent_map","get_comment_map","get_issuelinks_map","resolve_inbound_bridge_fields","_apply_inbound_create","_inbound_create_write_create_event","_ACLI_CEILING","SilentTruncationError","bridge_project","repos"],"problem_keywords":["multi-project inbound fetch","JQL fan-out","per-project enrichment","source-project recording","bridge_project","repos field","snapshot merging","inbound tickets"],"propositions":["The inbound fetcher currently queries only one tracker project and builds a single JQL pair, causing it to silently drop parent/comment/issuelink enrichment data for all projects except one in multi-project stores.","Inbound-created tickets do not record their source project, leaving bridge_project and repos fields unset.","The fetcher must fan out per-project JQL queries and run all three enrichment passes (parent, comment, issuelink maps) for each configured project, merging results into a shared snapshot deduplicated by seen_keys.","The truncation ceiling must remain scoped per project to prevent one busy project from exhausting a shared budget on behalf of others.","The source project for inbound tickets can be derived from the Jira key prefix, and repos can be resolved from the projects_store mapping for that project."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787775713594248001,"uuid":"5e89cbd0-4df0-4563-8912-34eeb35ce1c3"}